  "domain": "blockchain",
  "definition": "ERC-721 is the Ethereum token standard that defines the interface for non-fungible tokens (NFTs), where each token is uniquely identified by a uint256 token ID and an associated owner address recorded on-chain. Unlike ERC-20 fungible tokens, which are interchangeable, each ERC-721 token is distinct and cannot be exchanged equivalently for another. The standard defines a minimal interface including ownership transfer, approval delegation, and balance queries, plus an optional metadata extension that associates each token with a URI resolving to off-chain JSON metadata including name, description, and image. ERC-721 is the foundational standard for digital art, collectibles, gaming items, and tokenised real-world assets on Ethereum.",
